MappedParameterTwo = {
    ("EngagementCodeList", NAMEOF ( 'Project_snapshot_Fact'[EngagementCodeList] ), 0),
    ("AlphaCode", NAMEOF ( 'Project_snapshot_Fact'[AlphaCode] ), 1),
    ("CustodianDisplayName", NAMEOF ( 'Project_snapshot_Fact'[CustodianDisplayName] ), 2),
    ("EFileName", NAMEOF ( 'Project_snapshot_Fact'[EFileName] ), 3)
}
// A second, independent field parameter over the exact same 4 candidate
// columns as the aster plot's own MappedParameter (see
// visuals/aster-plot/dax/category-field-parameter.dax) -- lets a report
// viewer swap which column drives the waffle chart's Category role
// (bound to the visual's "Category2" role) via its own slicer,
// independently of whatever MappedParameter (bound to the "Category"
// role, feeding this visual's SeriesCategoryRaw) is currently sliced to.
//
// CONFIRMED LIVE (via a "view as table" screenshot with MappedParameter
// sliced to AlphaCode and MappedParameterTwo sliced to EngagementCodeList):
// Deneb exposes both roles as separate, simultaneous keys in the same
// row when they're sliced to different candidates -- no forced collision.
// But since both field parameters share the exact same 4 candidate names,
// and a field parameter's resolved key can't be renamed per-visual (same
// finding as MappedParameter, see category-field-parameter.dax), a naive
// isValid() cascade checking the same 4 candidates in the same order for
// both roles cannot tell them apart -- it will resolve BOTH roles to
// whichever candidate happens to be checked first and present, regardless
// of which field parameter it actually came from (reproduced locally
// before this was understood). The spec's field-mapping adapter
// (visuals/waffle-chart/spec/waffle-chart.vl.json) fixes this with an
// exclusion cascade: Category resolves first (highest-priority candidate
// present, same as always), then SeriesCategoryRaw resolves to the
// highest-priority *remaining* candidate that Category didn't already
// claim. See the README's "Field mapping" section for the full mechanism
// and the one scenario it can't disambiguate (both field parameters
// sliced to the identical column at the same time -- SeriesCategory
// safely falls back to "All" rather than showing a false duplicate).
//
// If you ever reference this table's own columns in a measure, use MAX,
// not SELECTEDVALUE or ALLSELECTED -- same composite-key constraint as
// MappedParameter, see visuals/aster-plot/dax/measure-a-color-gradient.dax
// for the full writeup. This table's own label column is CONFIRMED named
// "Category2" -- reference it as 'MappedParameterTwo'[Category2].
